{"title":"2019 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 24","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1_but_not_exactly\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1 but not exactly</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/0/1d020174f178fd1697cc16033099d4bcc6730e07.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega=-\\tfrac{1}{2}+\\tfrac{1}{2}i\\sqrt3.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"128\" height=\"23\" /> Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> denote all points in the complex plane of the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/6/876b2135bc8f88b4597609080624e6a9042f90f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b\\omega+c\\omega^2,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"105\" height=\"18\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/6/a3624c806aafa6e0ab9479030586ed99752a7421.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0\\leq a \\leq 1,0\\leq b\\leq 1,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"166\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/3/893be0caa16c25951a5cf0a4d7b8c6f1aa508248.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0\\leq c\\leq 1.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"78\" height=\"15\" /> What is the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/0/3c080677594faf8b15ab300cac7e92f3f784a379.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) } \\frac{1}{2}\\sqrt3 \\qquad\\textbf{(B) } \\frac{3}{4}\\sqrt3 \\qquad\\textbf{(C) } \\frac{3}{2}\\sqrt3\\qquad\\textbf{(D) } \\frac{1}{2}\\pi\\sqrt3 \\qquad\\textbf{(E) } \\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"478\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Notice that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/5/1859376c3119b46b0df33ad4782e7356a933798b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega=e^{\\frac{2i\\pi}{3}}$\" width=\"64\" height=\"18\" />, which is one of the cube roots of unity. We wish to find the span of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/8/08862f0282b094082fe81af6ed0687c59acf7ebb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a+b\\omega+c\\omega^2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"113\" height=\"19\" /> for reals <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/a/33a368b5e696a651413ceaa56952d6fca1c1e18e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0\\le a,b,c\\le 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"107\" height=\"16\" />.\nObserve also that if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/a/c7a0dc1d53202f0003849a81d76e5555b1ee251a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b,c&gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"74\" height=\"16\" />, then replacing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/1/c618e67306eeac0e6fd82a5a01b6f1e01863fb18.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a-\\min(a,b,c), b-\\min(a,b,c),$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"246\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/2/c525a419a7d0997c0e7351acc2e6fd25b3f4c0dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c-\\min(a,b,c)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"114\" height=\"18\" /> leaves the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/c/a2c306cd41c785559b6f695c535388cc49fe37c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b\\omega+c\\omega^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"103\" height=\"18\" /> unchanged. Therefore, assume that at least one of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/b/a5b29b358e825defa3e11b7d903d43ec31e5909a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b,c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"18\" /> is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. If exactly one of them is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, we can form an equilateral triangle of side length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> using the remaining terms. A similar argument works if exactly two of them are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. In total, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/0/be022135ddf62a9681b4578d3b21cdf6bd50120c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3+{3 \\choose 2} = 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"101\" height=\"53\" /> equilateral triangles, whose total area is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/3/8d3b4349c55465540850a1d2e14e655e67465aac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6 \\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} = \\boxed{\\textbf{(C) } \\frac{3}{2}\\sqrt3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"158\" height=\"48\" />.\n</p><p><i>Note</i>: A diagram of the six equilateral triangles is shown below.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/d/42dee9da6ce367a03187683e00b3061794ee81a5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(200,200); draw((0,0)--(1,0)--(1/2,sqrt(3)/2)--cycle); draw((0,0)--(1/2,sqrt(3)/2)--(-1/2,sqrt(3)/2)--cycle); draw((0,0)--(-1/2,sqrt(3)/2)--(-1,0)--cycle); draw((0,0)--(-1,0)--(-1/2,-sqrt(3)/2)--cycle); draw((0,0)--(-1/2,-sqrt(3)/2)--(1/2,-sqrt(3)/2)--cycle); draw((0,0)--(1/2,-sqrt(3)/2)--(1,0)--cycle); draw((-2,0)--(2,0)); draw((0,-2)--(0,2)); [/asy]\" width=\"335\" height=\"335\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1_but_not_exactly\">Solution 1 but not exactly</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1 but not exactly\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>WLOG <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> is the smallest of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Then the expression is equivalent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/6/de62b5b56658b304af387a24c775513727ea0033.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b\\omega$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" />. To find the area of the region, we need only consider the extremities (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/5/4559967057fa75539ffe05f49644a1d9248abc23.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=0, a=1, b=0, b=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"194\" height=\"18\" />), as they will form a polygon which contains all points. So, when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/7/85721af34098db413d50c6891430d81bf5b8663f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=0, b=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"91\" height=\"16\" /> we have the origin (diagram omitted). When <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/7/077804ce4e27bf17cd94bea69b102309859f90d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=1, b=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"94\" height=\"18\" /> we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/8/bc8bfcec4e893fce5af5bd604020203451a13995.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(100,100); draw((-2,0)--(2,0), gray); draw((0,-2)--(0,2), gray); draw((0,0)--(1,0), red); [/asy]\" width=\"168\" height=\"168\" />\n</p><p>When <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/7/6a7372a2f6167ca6f7e7a2bb7d5327f13c40d1d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=0, b=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"91\" height=\"16\" /> we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/a/6daadc8f563d24f943f940aa7bff08e6d351e3a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-\\frac{1}{2}, \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"62\" height=\"41\" />:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/6/926457dae1b29c096cd5fd0ecfb5319a318347ec.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(100,100); draw((-2,0)--(2,0), gray); draw((0,-2)--(0,2), gray); draw((0,0)--(-1/2,sqrt(3)/2), red); draw((0,0)--(1,0), red); [/asy]\" width=\"168\" height=\"168\" />\n</p><p>When <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/c/63c4192938291ec8d8c0743ef6e5bab78415469f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=1, b=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"91\" height=\"16\" /> we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/6/e36c583e5e885e56eacf8c989285ff116f21a374.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}, \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"51\" height=\"43\" />:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/6/8a62261bfd20fa77070b5f9733d01a63af411bf1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(100,100); draw((-2,0)--(2,0), gray); draw((0,-2)--(0,2), gray); draw((0,0)--(-1/2,sqrt(3)/2), red); draw((0,0)--(1,0), red); draw((-1/2,sqrt(3)/2)--(1/2,sqrt(3)/2), red); draw((1,0)--(1/2,sqrt(3)/2), red); [/asy]\" width=\"168\" height=\"168\" />\n</p><p>The area of this is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/9/4e9191a5007067cff8f6d73f4d3419e08238f00b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"26\" height=\"41\" />. Multiply this by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can add on each term one at a time. Firstly, the possible values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/d/1cde14c4fc4efc5fb89cb7fa564c49cdfa2b00aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textstyle c\\omega^2=c\\left(-\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}i\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"155\" height=\"32\" /> lie on the following line:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/2/8c2d83d684aa7536f13f6b53a82a041b1de44934.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(100,100); draw((0,0)--(-1/2,-sqrt(3)/2), blue); draw((-2,0)--(2,0)); draw((0,-2)--(0,2)); [/asy]\" width=\"168\" height=\"168\" />\n</p><p>For each point on the line, we can add <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/2/c522515d86502509bddfbeaaeb6c230a1c1177ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textstyle b\\omega=b\\left(-\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}i\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"148\" height=\"32\" />. This means that we can extend the area to\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/9/96983bc6c01c87d0af76515627bc8b76718003be.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(100,100); fill((0,0)--(-1/2,sqrt(3)/2)--(-1,0)--(-1/2,-sqrt(3)/2)--cycle, lightgray); draw((0,0)--(-1/2,sqrt(3)/2)--(-1,0)--(-1/2,-sqrt(3)/2)--cycle); draw((0,0)--(-1/2,sqrt(3)/2), red); draw((0,0)--(-1/2,-sqrt(3)/2), blue); draw((-2,0)--(2,0)); draw((0,-2)--(0,2)); [/asy]\" width=\"168\" height=\"168\" />\n</p><p>by \"moving\" the blue line along the red line. Finally, we can add <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> to every point, giving\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/9/b998688df0c98abb935726c2aeaf6d053c96694b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(100,100); fill((-1/2,sqrt(3)/2)--(-1,0)--(-1/2,-sqrt(3)/2)--(1/2,-sqrt(3)/2)--(1,0)--(1/2,sqrt(3)/2)--cycle, lightgray); draw((-1/2,sqrt(3)/2)--(-1,0)--(-1/2,-sqrt(3)/2)--(1/2,-sqrt(3)/2)--(1,0)--(1/2,sqrt(3)/2)--cycle); draw((0,0)--(-1/2,sqrt(3)/2), red); draw((0,0)--(-1/2,-sqrt(3)/2), blue); draw((-2,0)--(2,0)); draw((0,-2)--(0,2)); draw((0,0)--(1,0), heavygreen); [/asy]\" width=\"168\" height=\"168\" />\n</p><p>by \"moving\" the previous area along the green line. This leaves us with a regular hexagon with side length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, so, as in Solution 1, the total area is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/2/8c20ce2dff8969f5a41fd05a37649001b5df5e3f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C) } \\frac{3}{2}\\sqrt{3}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"84\" height=\"48\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_12B\" title=\"2019 AMC 12B\">2019 AMC 12B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_12B_Problems\" title=\"2019 AMC 12B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_12B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2019 AMC 12B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_23\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2019 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 23\">Problem 23</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2019 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 25\">Problem 25</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_1\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2019 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_2\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2019 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2019 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_4\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2019 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_5\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2019 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_12B_Prob